# Comment like OpenSees examples

Match the style of the public OpenSeesPy examples (RC frame EQ, laterally loaded pile, free-field effective stress, PM4Sand cyclic). The advisor must be able to read a block without guessing.

## Stages

Numbered headers with a divider, same grain as McGann/Shin site-response scripts:

```
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SOIL FOLLOW PILE/CAP (soil self-weight)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
```

State units once at the file top (N, m, s). Print when a stage finishes.

## Command syntax

Put the OpenSees argument list on the line above the call. Then say what *this* instance does (which nodes, which DOF, why).

```tcl
# equalDOF $rNodeTag $cNodeTag $dof1 $dof2
# soil UX,UY follow the coincident pile/cap under self-weight
equalDOF $retainNd $soilNd 1 2

# node $tag $x $y -mass $mx $my $mRz
node 3001 [expr {-$xSoffit}] $y0 -mass $deckM(BL) $deckM(BL) $deckIrot(BL)
```

Do not comment `wipe` / `analyze` as if the name were obscure. Do comment argument order (`pattern` tag vs dir, `rayleigh` four coefs, `equalDOF` retained vs constrained).

## Geometry and names

ASCII sketch with node names or tags when the layout is fixed (pile wiki sketch; our cap TL/ML grid, deck 3004--3006).

Full words: `soilNd`, `retainNd`. No leading `_`. `info exists` guards stay.

## Knobs

Group inputs with a unit and a short meaning (`CSR = 0.2  ;# cyclic stress ratio`). Cite API / Reese / Shin next to a formula, not a lecture.
